; AcpHal.def — ERA (Xbox One) audio-DSP-heap import lib (phase 5).
; The ACP is the console's audio DSP; desktop has no equivalent heap,
; so the layer answers these with explicit E_NOTIMPL stubs (logged) —
; see docs/ERA-GDK-MAPPING.md. Ordinals are WinDurango's AcpHal.dll
; ordinals (dumpbin /exports 2026-11-23): 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10.
; The FH2 exe's import table gives HINTS (0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9)
; — a hint is an index into the sorted export-name table, NOT an
; ordinal. (An earlier phase 5 note claimed AcpHalAllocateShapeContexts
; was ordinal 0 and could not be expressed in a .def — that was the
; hint, not the ordinal; its WinDurango ordinal is 1.) Signatures are
; XDK-gated; the stubs log their first four raw args.
LIBRARY AcpHal
EXPORTS
    AcpHalAllocateShapeContexts @1
    AcpHalCreate @2
    AcpHalReleaseShapeContexts @3
    ApuAlloc @4
    ApuCreateHeap @5
    ApuFree @6
    ApuIsVirtualAddressValid @8
    ApuMapApuAddress @9
    ApuMapVirtualAddress @10
